      "hadithIndex": 2670,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that a man said:\"O Messenger of Allah, what clothes should we wear when we enter Ihram?\" He said: \"Do not wear a shirt (or shirts), or 'Imamahs, or pants, or Khuffs unless someone Cannot find sandals, in which case he should cut them (the Khuffs) so that they come beneath the ankles or any garment that has been touched by (dyed with ) wars or saffron",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1321-24-2670-abughuddah",
          "name": "Abu Ghuddah",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
