      "bookIndex": 24,
      "hadithIndex": 2676,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said; \"A man came to the Prophet and said:'What should we wear when we enter Ihram?' He said: 'Do not wear a shirt, or an 'Imamah, or pants, or a burnouts, or Khuffs unless you cannot find any sandals. If you cannot find any sandals, then wear something that comes beneath the ankles",
      "grades": [
        {
